export anchor SpectrumAnalyserStyle:
    number: 325
    screen: MusicPlayer
    name: Spectrum analyser
    idea: The bars and peak caps of a live frequency analyser run the whole layout, so every figure on the page, from progress to volume to song length, is drawn as lime and cyan level bars on black.
    base: dark
    palette:
        void: #040605, the page, the analyser well and the style sheet
        well: #0a110c, panels and readout strips
        grid: #1b2b20, graticule lines, unlit segments and panel borders
        phosphor: #e3f4e6, text
        dim: #8fa897, labels, units and axis text
        lime: #b8ff3d, analyser bars, lit progress segments, the lyric marker and focus
        cyan: #46e6ff, peak caps, song length bars, the volume segments and the liked control
        onLime: #0b1400, text on lime
    type:
        One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas,
        Liberation Mono. Base 14px at 1.5. The title is 40px at 700 in caps
        with 0.02em tracking, readouts 16px at 700 in lime with tabular
        figures, rows 14px, caps labels 12px with 0.14em tracking and axis
        figures 11px.
    layout:
        A test instrument. A ruled header strip reads BRIGHTWORK SOUND in
        lime then Analyser, with CH A+B and Now playing on the right. Under
        it a full width analyser well 260px tall draws 32 lime bars with a
        darker base and a cyan peak cap above each, over faint graticule
        lines, with dB marks down the right edge. The title box sits in the
        top left corner of the well, black with ruled edges, holding Now
        playing, HARBOUR LIGHTS and the artist with the album dimmed. A
        frequency scale from 31 to 16k Hz runs under the well. A transport
        strip follows, with 02 14 in lime, a 48 segment progress bar lit
        to just under half and 04 38, then square buttons each with an icon
        over a short caps word, SHUF, PREV, a lime PAUSE, NEXT, RPT and a
        cyan outlined LIKED with a filled heart. A LEVEL row shows ten
        cyan segments with seven lit and 70%. Three ruled panels close the
        screen. Up next lists numbered rows whose cyan bar length is the
        song length, Src library gives each playlist a lime bar sized by
        song count plus caps links for Albums, Artists and Podcasts, and
        Lyrics shows the current line bold behind a lime chevron with a
        NOW tag and the next line dim. Below 980px the queue takes a full
        row, and below 640px the title box moves under the bars, the
        progress shows 24 segments and everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 2px gaps between segments and bars, 16px panel padding and 16px between panels.
    density: High. Readouts, scales and segment meters fill every panel like test gear.
    corners: None. Every bar, segment, button and panel is square.
    borders: 1px grid lines around every panel and behind the analyser. Coloured borders appear only on the liked control and on focus.
    shadows: None, apart from a faint lime glow of 6px at 35 percent under the analyser bars.
    icons:
        Solid square cut transport glyphs above a four letter caps word.
        Liked uses a filled heart and the word LIKED. The current lyric
        line uses a chevron and a NOW tag. Bars always sit beside the
        figure they draw.
    focus: A 2px lime outline offset 2px plus a lime corner tick at the bottom right.
    tone: Instrument labels in caps, such as CH A+B, LEVEL, UP NEXT and SRC LIBRARY.
